Dear Corine, Bert and Vikas

Thank you, I have now merged the latest translation into the Dutch User=C2=
=B4s guide.

I have used most of the day to update my internal documentation of the rele=
ase process and it

looks like I'll be able to create the official release tomorrow in due time=
 to give it to Bo on an USB stick,

so he can bring it to his conference in Vejle.

 

As far as I know the conference is for teachers within the blind- and weakl=
y sighted area, but I'll cc Bo

on this so maybe he can tell you more details.

 

You're right, I never told you how this project is organized:

Bo works as a normal employee at IBOS. His job is to help blind and weakly =
sighted people in relation to jobs.

I myself work at IBOS on part time, typically one or 2 days per week and ty=
pically for 3 or 4 months in the winter time.

I am partly retired and have to follow some very strict Danish employment-r=
ules: Every hour  I work, even for free, will cost me about 7 Euro. So I on=
ly work when funding is available, typical from private organizations. That=
 is why I cannot work after January 31.

After that time Bo and I (and the IBOS administration) will have to discuss=
 the future of the project. We have some ideas, but we need support from th=
e IBOS organization.

The story about "Corine and Bert and Vikas in Holland successfully translat=
ing the IBOS MusicXmlReader to Dutch" is actually "gefundenes fressen" for =
us because it proves to the IBOS organization that people out there are rea=
lly interested in the project.

And I agree: The process of translating the program into another language r=
equires a lot of skills, but typically dedicated users of the program - as =
you - already possess these skills, so we hope to get more translations now=
 when we know how to do it and how long time it takes.

I guess that as you have sent us your photos we can use them (and the story=
) when we try to spread the news about the MusicXmlReader ? 

And yes, let's keep in contact, I'll send you a link the  new version when =
it is more officially released.

Best regards

Jens

 

 

 

 

 

 

 

 

 

 

